#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: 8 lemons 22
#> pause: 40
#> must: 1 APPLES 12
#> must: 6 GRAPES 40
#> must: 3 cherries 7 <- untouched
#> not: APPLES 12 <-
#> source: t
# 12. t. Sheet: "t label" branches to the label if the last substitute modified the
# pattern space. The first s/// upper-cases the fruit on lines with an a. t then
# branches to the end only on those lines; the ones where s/// made no change fall
# through and get the arrow. t is how sed loops: ":a;s/x/y/;ta" runs until s fails.
# Try: replace t with "b": the arrow disappears everywhere, changed or not.
s/\([a-z]*a[a-z]*\)/\U\1/
t
s/$/ <- untouched/

#DATA
1 apples 12
2 bananas 30
3 cherries 7
4 dates 16
5 figs 25
6 grapes 40
7 kiwis 18
8 lemons 22
